// demos/mcplay/main.fi -- playable prototype: joins a Minecraft server (offline mode), opens a window, renders the streamed world
// and lets you walk / fly, break and place blocks.
//
//   mcplay <host-ipv4> <port> <name>
//
// Controls: mouse look (captured), W A S D, Space (jump / up), Shift (sneak / down), Ctrl (sprint), 1-9 / wheel (hotbar),
// LMB break (creative: instant, otherwise hold MCPLAY_DIG_MS), RMB place, F fly on/off, N noclip, F11 fullscreen, Esc release the
// mouse (click captures again), Alt+F4 / window close quits.
//
// Environment (all optional):
//   MCPLAY_GL=1        GL path (not wired yet: see docs/mc/play.md; the demo then says so and uses the CPU path)
//   MCPLAY_VIEW=6      view distance in chunks            MCPLAY_PROTOCOL=763   protocol number
//   MCPLAY_W / MCPLAY_H window size (default 854x480)     MCPLAY_FULLSCREEN=1   start fullscreen
//   MCPLAY_FPS=60      frame cap (0 = uncapped)           MCPLAY_VSYNC=1        swap interval for the GL path (CPU path: no-op)
//   MCPLAY_CREATIVE=1  the server is creative: fly allowed and the creative reach (6 blocks)
//   MCPLAY_TICKS=2000  time of day until the first update_time packet arrives (then the server time drives the sky)
//   MCPLAY_LIGHT=1     vertex light (mc_wlight: Chunk.light + 5x5 column region, edits repair it) + sky daylight uniform; 0 = old flat tint
//   sound: MCPLAY_SOUNDS=<dir with bank.json + wavs> (default $HOME/.cache/mcplay/sounds; made by tools/sounds/gen tools/sounds/mc.json <dir>)
//          FIRN_AUDIO=file:/x.wav|null|device (default device); MCPLAY_AUDIO=0 off; MCPLAY_VOL_<MASTER|BLOCKS|AMBIENT|PLAYERS|HOSTILE|NEUTRAL|MUSIC|UI>=0..100; M = mute
//   packs: MC_PACKS / MC_PACK_CONFIG / MC_PACK_AUTO (see docs/mc/resourcepacks.md); T = hot reload, animated tiles tick at 20 Hz
//   MCPLAY_DIG_MS=700  hold time before the "finish digging" packet in survival (there is no hardness table yet)
//   MCPLAY_PLACE_ID=0  block state id painted locally on a place click (0 = wait for the server's Block Update)
//   MCPLAY_RUN_S=0     quit after N seconds (tests)       MCPLAY_SHOT=<file.png>  write the last frame as PNG on exit + print its hash
//   MCPLAY_AUDIO=0     sound: 0 off, 1 on (FIRN_AUDIO=null|file:<path>|device selects the sink)
//
// Frame order: pump events -> network (chunks, block updates) -> 20 Hz ticks (movement, position packets) -> pick -> mouse actions ->
// clear, sky, world, light tint, selection box, HUD -> present. Packets are applied as they arrive: Block Update / Multi Block
// Change change the world (mc_blockset) and dirty the mesh cache (wr_mark_block).
